<h2>Indian sesame seeds for export</h2>
<p>India became the world's largest sesame seed exporter in 2023, supplying hulled and natural seed into three quite distinct demand streams: East Asian food manufacturing, Western bakery and health-food channels, and oil crushing.</p>

<p>We supply hulled (dehulled white), natural white and natural black sesame at purity grades up to 99.95%, machine-cleaned, sortex-sorted and metal-detected, from Gujarat, Rajasthan, West Bengal and Madhya Pradesh.</p>

<h2>Hulled or natural — which do you need?</h2>
<p>This is the first question to settle, because the two are different products at different prices:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Hulled sesame</strong> has the seed coat mechanically removed. Whiter, softer, used in bakery toppings, confectionery and tahini. Commands a premium. Shorter shelf life — the exposed oil oxidises faster, so storage temperature matters more.</li>
  <li><strong>Natural sesame</strong> retains the coat. Preferred for oil crushing (better yield economics) and for applications where the coat's flavour and mineral content are wanted.</li>
  <li><strong>Natural black sesame</strong> is a separate market again, mostly East Asian confectionery and culinary use.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How purity grades work</h2>
<p>Purity is the percentage of clean, sound sesame in the lot after cleaning — 99%, 99.5% and 99.95% are the standard export tiers. Getting to 99.95% requires sortex colour-sorting and tighter cleaning, which costs more. Japanese and European food buyers typically want 99.95%; crushers are often content with 99%. Paying for 99.95% when you're going to crush it is money spent on a specification you won't use.</p>

<h2>Testing matters more on sesame than most products</h2>
<p>Sesame has been the subject of significant residue and contamination controls in the EU, Japan and Korea in recent years. For those destinations, pre-shipment aflatoxin and pesticide residue testing is strongly advisable — a rejection at destination on a container of sesame is an expensive lesson. We arrange testing on request; tell us your destination market early so the right panel is used. {{ site.inspectionStatement }}</p>

